\frametitle{Browser-facing validation path}
\protect\phantomsection\label{browser-facing-validation-path}
For end-to-end browser validation, open the dashboard, confirm the
official SkillTree panel mounts the \texttt{activeInference} project,
switch to the curriculum panel, and open a skill's \textbf{Learn},
\textbf{Open Subject}, and \textbf{Quiz} actions. \textbf{Learn} opens
the local modular lesson record and should not emit a direct
\texttt{/subjects/\{subjectId\}/skills/\{skillId\}} SkillTree target.
\textbf{Open Subject} reopens the dashboard with
\texttt{skillsClientDisplayPath=/subjects/\{subjectId\}} so the subject
learning path, skill list, progress, and rank are exercised inside the
official SkillTree display. \textbf{Quiz} opens
\texttt{skillsClientDisplayPath=/subjects/\{subjectId\}/skills/\{skillId\}/quizzes/\{quizId\}},
so quiz loading, scoring rules, and completion remain SkillTree-owned
rather than dashboard-owned.
